WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.080
Okay, so an agent loop is four phases,

2
00:00:03.080 --> 00:00:07.667
and a failure in any one looks like the whole agent failing.

3
00:00:07.667 --> 00:00:09.167
First it perceives,

4
00:00:09.167 --> 00:00:10.387
reading its context,

5
00:00:10.387 --> 00:00:11.587
then it thinks,

6
00:00:11.587 --> 00:00:13.087
deciding which tool to call,

7
00:00:13.087 --> 00:00:14.247
and then it acts,

8
00:00:14.247 --> 00:00:15.333
calling that tool.

9
00:00:15.333 --> 00:00:16.673
Last, it remembers,

10
00:00:16.673 --> 00:00:18.813
updating its state with the result,

11
00:00:18.813 --> 00:00:21.900
so the next cycle has accurate context.

12
00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:23.960
Each phase fails in its own way,

13
00:00:23.960 --> 00:00:26.380
so infinite loops start in act,

14
00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:28.633
and lost tool results start in remember.

15
00:00:28.633 --> 00:00:31.233
So I'd check perceive first,

16
00:00:31.233 --> 00:00:37.373
then remember, because what reads as bad reasoning can be a perception or memory problem.
